From ec4d41f119356808dea107f6ca9e551e2b60c5c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:37:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kernel config: nf_tables, SCTP, VXLAN, the IPv6 rt match and
 five unused matches off (102.8 line)

Code that nothing on the router uses, taken out of the kernel and its modules:
- nf_tables and its ARP family: both iptables builds are configured without nftables and no
  program, module or amtm add-on (36 checked from source) uses it. Closes CVE-2024-1086 (CISA KEV)
  and 28 more nf_tables CVEs.
- SCTP sockets (IP_SCTP) and VXLAN: no user in rc, any module or any add-on. SCTP passing through
  the router is still tracked (NF_CT_PROTO_SCTP and xt_sctp stay); WireGuard keeps its UDP tunnel
  support.
- The IPv6 routing-header match (IP6_NF_MATCH_RT): no rule uses -m rt. release/src/Makefile forced
  it on whenever IPv6 was enabled.
- The ipp2p, webmon, web, geoip and condition matches: no rule or program loads them.
config_base.6a.6813 is the kernel config of every model; .4916 is kept in step. CIFS stays: amtm
backup add-ons mount SMB shares with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
